# Web SEO: Programmatic SEO (pSEO)

Programmatic routes ship **catalog constants** on the server, **SSR meta + JSON-LD** in `+page.server.ts`, and **templates** in `+page.svelte`. SSR meta, canonical, and JSON-LD mechanics: **web-seo-meta-tags**, **web-seo-canonical**, **web-seo-jsonld**.

Landing (`/`) and pricing FAQ: **web-seo-cms-copy** + **web-landing-faqs**. Hub and detail pages: **tailored** FAQ constants plus shared git-default rows via `appendPublicGeneralFaqItems` (**web-landing-faqs**). URL → folder map and canonical imports: `web/src/content/docs/getting-started-for-dev/architecture.md` (Marketing copy section).

## Three-layer contract

| Layer | Location | Responsibility |
| --- | --- | --- |
| **Constants** | `web/src/lib/content/constants/**` (and feature `*/constants/` for tool-specific marketing) | Hero, features, FAQ Q&A, meta strings, hub blurbs — import canonical modules (`channels/index.ts`, `agents/index.ts`, `mcps/index.ts`, `hubs/*.ts`, `faq/index.ts`, `channels/api/index.ts`) |
| **Server load** | `+page.server.ts` | `createMetaData`, `buildCanonicalUrl`, `schemaData` (`createPublicFaqSEOSchema`, domain builders), VMs from presenters |
| **Template** | `+page.svelte` | `$derived(data.*)`; `<JsonLdHead schemaData={…} />`; `<PublicFaq … />`; no inline JSON-LD |

Forward `pageMetaTags` and `schemaData` through universal `+page.ts` on client nav (**web-sveltekit-universal-page-load**).

Public programmatic routes render in `+page.svelte` — **no** thin `*Page.svelte` wrappers that only forward props (**web-conventions** §7).

## pSEO content tiers (where per-channel files live)

Pick the tier by route family. Tier 1 and Tier 2 both use a `platforms/{slug}.ts` file per network (different VM types and parent folders).

| Tier | Routes | Module pattern | File shape |
| --- | --- | --- | --- |
| **1 — Channel identity** | `/channels/{slug}` | `channels/catalog/platforms/{slug}.ts` | **Full** `PublicChannelLandingPageViewModel`; register in `catalog/seeds.ts`. Shared catalog infra: `catalog/types.ts`, `shared.ts`, `feature-bento.ts`. WhoIsFor: `audienceCards` (3) + optional `audienceTailoredCard`; `resolvePublicChannelAudienceCards` in `channels/index.ts` for agent/API surfaces |
| **2 — API marketing** | `/social-media-posting-api/{slug}`, scheduling sibling | `channels/api/posting/platforms/{slug}.ts` | **Full** platform page VM (`buildPublicApiPlatformPage`). Export **both** posting and scheduling VMs from the same file; `api/scheduling/index.ts` imports scheduling exports only (no `api/scheduling/platforms/`) |
| **3 — Derived tools** | `/tools/{tool}/{slug}` | `channels/tool-surfaces/{slug}.ts` + `tools/{tool}/general.ts` | **Sparse** `ChannelToolContentOverride` merged via `mergeChannelToolContentOverride`; register in that tool’s `CHANNEL_CONTENT_OVERRIDES` |

**Tier 3 (tools only):** `tools/{tool}/general.ts` derives defaults from `listAvailablePublicChannels()`. Per-network copy lives in `channels/tool-surfaces/{slug}.ts` (`{slug}ToolSurfaceMeta`). Registry: `tool-surfaces/shared/channelToolSurfaceRegistry.ts`. Each slug gets best-time `seoIntro` + benchmark table (from `benchmarkSlots.ts`), photo-editor preset copy (aligned with `aspectRatioPresets.ts`), and skill-builder FAQs (aligned with `CHANNEL_RECIPES` + `agent/skills/openquok-core` CLI examples). Maps: `bestTimeToolContentOverridesBySlug` et al. in `tool-surfaces/index.ts`.

**No `agent-surfaces` / `mcp-surfaces` under `channels/`:** Tier 3 is **channel-keyed patches on tool shells**. Agents and MCPs live under `agents/` and `mcps/` and **compose** `channels/catalog` — host-first or client-first, not per-network files under `channels/`.

| URL | Where to edit |
| --- | --- |
| `/agents/{host}` (skill host) | `agents/hosts/{host}.ts` |
| `/agents/{mcpSlug}` (MCP client) | `mcps/hosts/{mcpSlug}.ts` |
| `/agents/{host}/{channelSlug}` | `agents/channels/{host}.ts` + `channels/catalog/platforms/{channelSlug}.ts` |
| `/agents/{mcpSlug}/{channelSlug}` | `mcps/hosts/{mcpSlug}.ts` + `channels/catalog/platforms/{channelSlug}.ts` + `buildMcpChannelLandingVm.ts`; hub/routing: `agents/channels/index.ts` — **map:** `mcps/channels/index.ts` (no `mcps/channels/{channelSlug}.ts` seeds) |

Do not add `agents/channels/{socialSlug}.ts` unless one host×channel needs copy that cannot live in the host template or catalog.

Inventory: `web/src/lib/content/constants/_dev/programmatic-landing/publicProgrammaticLandingRegistry.ts`.

**Naming:** `content/constants/landing/` is shared home/hub chrome (CTAs, breadcrumbs) — not `/channels/{slug}`. `self-hosting/landing.ts` is only `/self-hosting`. Channel identity is always `channels/catalog/platforms/{slug}.ts` (import via `channels/index.ts`).

