## JSON-LD in templates

- **Only** `<JsonLdHead schemaData={schemaData} />` — `schemaData` from load (`$derived(data.schemaData)`).
- **No** inline `<script type="application/ld+json">` or object literals in `+page.svelte` (**web-seo-jsonld**).

## FAQ blocks

```svelte
<PublicFaq
  faqSubtitle={faqSubtitle}
  faqTitle={faqTitle}
  faqDescription={faqDescription}
  faqItems={[...faqItems]}
/>
```

- Items: `{ title: string; description: string; id?: PublicFaqItemId }` — `description` is HTML from `faqLink` helpers.
- `FaqAccordion` runs `prepareBlogRichTextForDisplay` + `rewriteHtmlHostedMarketingHrefs` before render.
- Hub configs: spread readonly arrays (`[...PUBLIC_CHANNELS_HUB_FAQ.faqItems]`) when passing to `PublicFaq`. Lists are **tailored + appended** git-default rows — see **web-landing-faqs** (do not replace hub copy with id-only subsets).

## Guest mocks (tools)

Public tool UIs mock workspace features without OAuth or post APIs:

- `pointer-events-none` on mock shells; lock toolbars clickable (**web-public-auth-funnel**).
- Label samples as preview — not “Connected channels”.
- Channel-specific tool routes preselect the matching mock channel.

## Landing and FAQ copy — ASD-STE100

Every pSEO FAQ answer **and** user-facing landing string (channel, agent, MCP, tool, hub config: heroes, hub blurbs, feature descriptions, audience cards) must use **ASD-STE100 Simplified Technical English**:

- Short sentences; one idea per sentence.
- Active voice; second person when addressing the reader (`you`, `your workspace`).
- Approved, plain vocabulary — avoid jargon stacks and passive spec lists.
- **Do not** meta-comment in user-facing copy (never write “this answer uses STE100”).

Feature **titles** may keep comma-split lines for hero theme. **Descriptions** still follow STE100.

Questions stay plain text; answers are HTML fragments from `faqLink` / `faqLinkSelfHostChannelSetup`. New agent/MCP hosts: **add-agent**. New channels: **add-social-provider-integration**.

## FAQ link helpers (`publicFaqLinks.ts`)

| Export | Use |
| --- | --- |
| `faqLink(href, label)` | Root-relative `<a href="…">` — no `rel="nofollow"` on first-party paths |
| `publicFaqHref` | Shared destinations: `signUp`, `connectChannelsGuide`, `pricing`, `channels`, `tools`, `compare`, CLI/docs hubs, etc. |
| `faqLinkSelfHostChannelSetup(docsPath, platformLabel)` | Operator setup under `/docs/social-integration/{slug}` — anchor **must** include `self-host` |
| `buildChannelFaqLinks`, `buildAgentFaqLinks`, `buildToolChannelFaqLinks` | Per-slug landing, tag hub, and docs hrefs |

Rules for all pSEO FAQ answers:

- Root-relative `href="/…"`; one or two links per destination per answer.
- JSON-LD parity: `createPublicFaqSEOSchema` uses the same Q&A; `Answer.text` is plain text (link labels kept, tags stripped) after `prepareBlogRichTextForDisplay` — same pipeline as `FaqAccordion`.

## Channel connect FAQ funnel

On OpenQuok Cloud, developer apps are already registered; users **sign up** and use **Add channel** in the workspace (`/docs/channels/connect`). Self-host operator docs are allowed but **secondary** and must be labeled.

| Doc path | Audience | FAQ usage |
| --- | --- | --- |
| `/docs/channels/connect` | End users (cloud + dashboard) | **Primary** link for “how do I connect” |
| `/sign-up`, `/pricing` | Trial and plan limits | **Primary** CTA on connect and trial questions |
| `/docs/social-integration/{slug}` | Self-host operators (env vars, developer apps) | **Secondary**; prose or anchor must say **self-host** |
| `/docs/cli-examples/{slug}` | Automation | After connect, for API/CLI questions |

**Priority order** in connect / OAuth FAQ answers:

1. **Sign up** — `publicFaqHref.signUp` (free trial where true).
2. **Connect in workspace** — Add channel steps or `publicFaqHref.connectChannelsGuide`.
3. **Self-host only (optional, one sentence)** — `faqLinkSelfHostChannelSetup(docsPath, platformLabel)`.

```ts
// ❌ BAD — social-integration as primary “setup guide”
`Follow the ${faqLink(youtubeLinks.docs, 'YouTube setup guide')}.`

// ✅ GOOD — sign-up first; self-host labeled
`${faqLink(publicFaqHref.signUp, 'Sign up for free')}, open a workspace, and choose Connect channel → YouTube. … For self-hosted deployments, see the ${faqLinkSelfHostChannelSetup('/docs/social-integration/youtube', 'YouTube')}.`
```

**Forbidden:**

- “Follow the {Platform} setup guide” → `social-integration` without `self-host` in the anchor.
- Implying cloud users must register Meta/Google/TikTok developer apps or set backend env vars.
- Bare `{Platform} setup guide` anchor text for any `/docs/social-integration/` href.

`buildChannelFaqLinks(…).docs` resolves operator paths — use only with `faqLinkSelfHostChannelSetup`, not as the primary connect CTA.

