## Footer inventory (`PUBLIC_FOOTER_LINKS`)

Sitewide footer columns in `web/src/lib/config/constants/config.ts`. Hub-level links (Tools, Resources, Company, Directories) are static; **per-channel/per-doc rows** are built in `web/src/lib/config/utils/buildPublicFooterLinks.ts` from catalogs and docs frontmatter — see **add-social-provider-integration** → **Site footer** when shipping a social channel (do not hand-edit footer rows per slug).

| Column | Examples |
| --- | --- |
| **Tools** | `/tools`, `/tools/skill-builder`, `/tools/photo-editor`, `/tools/humanizer`, `/tools/best-time-to-post` |
| **Skill Builder / Photo Editor / Humanizer / Best Time to Post Tools** | Auto: `/tools/{tool}/{channelSlug}` from live channel catalogs |
| **Supported Channels** | Auto: `/channels/{slug}` from `listPublicChannelLandingSeedsForFooter()` (`channels/catalog/seeds.ts`) |
| **Social Media Posting / Scheduling API** | Auto: `/social-media-posting-api/{slug}` and `/social-media-scheduling-api/{slug}` from `listPublicApiPostingPlatformsForHub()` / `listPublicApiSchedulingPlatformsForHub()` |
| **How to self-host with different social channels** | Auto: `/docs/social-integration/{slug}` from setup-guide markdown |
| **Autonomous Agent / MCP Integrations** | Auto: `/agents/{slug}` from agent/MCP catalogs |
| **API Payload Validators / Integrations APIs / …** | Auto: `/docs/apis-*` from `docsSidebarPublicApi` + operation markdown |
| **Directories** | `/playbooks`, `/building-blocks`, `/creators`, category/tag index paths |
| **Resources** | `/agents`, `/channels`, `/alternatives`, `/blog`, `/compare`, `/docs`, self-host install |
| **Company** | `/about`, `/roadmap`, `/pricing`, Discord |

New pSEO routes that should be discoverable from every page belong here or in header nav config — not only in FAQ cross-links. Add a static hub row in `config.ts` or extend `buildPublicFooterLinks.ts` when introducing a **new column type**; individual channel slugs stay catalog-driven.

## PR checklist (pSEO)

- [ ] FAQ answers and landing copy (hero, hub, feature descriptions, audience) follow ASD-STE100 (short, active, one idea per sentence).
- [ ] Connect questions: sign-up and/or connect guide before operator docs.
- [ ] Any `/docs/social-integration/` link uses `faqLinkSelfHostChannelSetup` or anchor text containing `self-host`.
- [ ] `publicFaqLinks.test.ts` + channel-level tests: `href="/sign-up"` or connect guide on connect FAQs; no unlabeled social-integration anchors.
- [ ] Hub FAQ wired: tailored constants + `appendPublicGeneralFaqItems` (**web-landing-faqs**) → `createPublicFaqSEOSchema` in `+page.server.ts` → `PublicFaq` in `+page.svelte` → forward in `+page.ts`.
- [ ] Template section order matches surfaces above; no thin `*Page.svelte` wrappers (**web-conventions** §7).
- [ ] JSON-LD `Answer.text` matches visible accordion (no raw `<a>` tags).
- [ ] Meta + canonical + JSON-LD `url` use the same `buildCanonicalUrl` (**web-seo-canonical**).

